  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.60:\n\t\t- Fixed: an unrecognised LogicModule type no longer deserialises to LogicModuleType.All, the\n\t\t  value that means \"every type\" when querying. A type this client did not model was therefore\n\t\t  indistinguishable from a deliberate no-filter, so a caller grouping by Type either dropped\n\t\t  those modules or filed them under a heading that means nothing, with nothing to indicate\n\t\t  anything was missing. TolerantStringEnumConverter already resolved an unmatched value to a\n\t\t  member named Unknown and fell back to All only in its absence; LogicModuleType now has one.\n\t\t  The converter itself is unchanged, and All remains 0, so the no-filter sentinel and\n\t\t  default(LogicModuleType) are unaffected for existing callers.\n\t\t- Added: LogicModuleType.RemediationSource, for LogicMonitor's remote action modules - Kill\n\t\t  Windows Process, Restart Linux Device, Microsoft Windows Disk Cleanup, Suspend and Resume\n\t\t  Windows Server Cluster Node and similar. The wire value is REMEDIATIONSOURCE, not the\n\t\t  ACTIONSOURCE the module names suggest. On one live portal nine such modules were landing on\n\t\t  All, out of 4,234 returned by setting/logicmodules/metadata.",
